      "message": "If init is called during the normal boot process, there won\u0027t be any data to restore, since data only gets saved pre-sysjump.  That\u0027s not really an error.\n\n(We currently ignore the return codes from hooks so this doesn\u0027t hurt anything yet, but someday we may pay attention to them.)\n\nSuggest changing this to:\n\nif (prev \u0026\u0026 version \u003d\u003d KB_HOOK_VERSION \u0026\u0026 size \u003d\u003d sizeof(*prev)) {\n   // Coming back from a sysjump, so restore settings\n   ...\n}\n\nreturn EC_SUCCESS;",
